  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "From our 44 pancreatic tumour expression profiles, motif prior and PPI table, I want each TF's activity in each tumour. I also want a model that predicts which new patients will respond to chemotherapy."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want each TF's activity in each tumour.\" -- available from GIRAFFE.\n2. \"I also want a model that predicts which new patients will respond to chemotherapy.\" -- not available here: no registered workflow produces this. No registered workflow fits a predictive or generative model; per-sample results can only be features for one built elsewhere.\n\nAbout \"I also want a model that predicts which new patients will respond to chemotherapy.\": No registered workflow builds a model that predicts an outcome for new samples. Per-sample results -- targeting scores from per-sample networks, GIRAFFE's TF activities, or subtypes -- can serve as features for a classifier you build outside NetZoo, which then needs the outcome for each sample and testing on samples not used to build it.\n\n**GIRAFFE**. GIRAFFE jointly factors expression into a regulatory-effect matrix and sample-varying TF activities using biological priors. Signed effects describe the fitted activation/repression relationship, while activity differs from the TF's own expression. These fitted coefficients do not alone establish causality.\n\nYou would need expression matrix, motif/prior, PPI network. The analysis would provide inferred regulator-to-target associations; inferred transcription-factor-by-sample activity values.\n\nFor “predict which new patients will respond to chemotherapy”, no registered workflow meets the stated requirement. That part needs a clearer measurement or an external method.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran.\n\nWhat measurement would let you distinguish the remaining explanation?"
    }
  ],
